# A host's malformed `CallError.code` is rewritten, and counted.
#
#   "Transport-Timeout"  malformed ([LECC.1.2]: uppercase, a hyphen): enters
#                        as `internal.invariant`, counted once, before the
#                        assert's tick (libds rewrites before it samples)
#   "transport.timeout"  well-formed: enters as given, nothing counted
#   "timeout"            one segment: well-formed by [LECC.1.2]'s pattern,
#                        the check both runtimes make, though [LECC.1.3]
#                        calls a one-segment adapter code malformed; it
#                        enters as given
#
# Each CallError takes its own correlation, so none supersedes another
# ([LCRS.6.2.4]) and each is logged by `seen` with the code it carries.
# @spec [LECC.1.5]
assert CallError corr="c1" code="Transport-Timeout" message="m" ts=0
pump
assert CallError corr="c2" code="transport.timeout" message="m" ts=0
pump
assert CallError corr="c3" code="timeout" message="m" ts=0
pump
